is to fill gaps along the gamma curve at the D=3.3852 corner, since the rest of the front is already dense.\",\n\"evidence\": [\n\"C-6daecae7b30e (-1.5°): flux 227200 W/m2, T 417.87 K. C-c2d1addc0c7e (-1.75°): 232230 W/m2, 413.81 K. The gap between them is the largest on the front and has no evaluated points at D=3.3852.\",\n\"C-7fa59b50781c (-2.0°): 237570 W/m2, 409.98 K. C-60b626663373 (-2.5°): 248980 W/m2, 403.04 K. The interval from -2.0 to -2.5 is sparsely sampled at D=3.3852.\",\n\"C-8efe13d24286 (-3.5703°, D=3.385) has max_g 12.0000, margin 3.2e-5. C-96e48a93fd32 (-3.5695°, D=3.3852) has margin 1.2e-4. C-112b974177e0 (-3.572°) is infeasible on max_g, so gamma is capped near -3.5703.\",\n\"C-4e45b26ae0a9, C-166a3a760ccb, C-3d41ce848a30, C-dcc9bfd9f503, C-bcce2808c9b8 and C-2375647d7e43 all failed on cd_fore extrapolation. C-ed967979f72a failed on geometry. No bluntness or cone change should be attempted.\",\n\"D=3.3852 shows a mass-fraction margin of 2.677e-5 against 1.449e-4 at D=3.385, and flux and T are marginally better at the larger D. Every proposal therefore keeps D=3.3852, inherited from the parent.\"\n],\n\"mechanism\": \"This relies on the data and on prior Allen-Eggers-type reasoning. Peak flux scales roughly as sqrt(sin(gamma)) and rises with steeper entry. The heat pulse shortens with steeper entry, so bondline T falls. Peak g rises with gamma and sets the steep limit. Locally, flux and T are smooth and nearly linear in gamma. The proposals interpolate between evaluated neighbours at D=3.3852 (slopes about +20 to +24 kW/m2 per degree in flux and -12 to -16 K per degree in T). This adds coverage of the trade-off curve without any surrogate-hull or geometry risk.\",\n\"uncertainty\": \"Interpolated flux and T should be accurate to well under 0.3% because the curve is smooth. The main risk is the two points nearest the g limit (-3.565°, -3.57°), where max_g margin is around 1e-4. This is a reduced-order model and I have not seen behaviour beyond the evaluated range. Expected hypervolume gain is very small (about 1e-5).\",\n\"proposals\": [\n{\n\"parent_id\": \"C-6daecae7b30e\",\n\"rationale\": \"Fill the largest gap on the shallow end of the front, between -1.5° and -1.75°.\",\n\"parameter_changes\": {\"flight_path_angle_deg\": -1.6},\n\"expected_outcome\": {\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\": 229200, \"peak_bondline_temperature_k\": 416.2, \"feasible\": true},\n\"uncertainty\": \"low\",\n\"reason_to_simulate\": \"Adds a front point in the widest gap; the linear interpolation is well constrained by the neighbours.\",\n\"requested_fidelity\": 0\n},\n{\n\"parent_id\": \"C-6daecae7b30e\",\n\"rationale\": \"A second point in the -1.5° to -1.75° gap, so the shallow end of the curve is captured.\",\n\"parameter_changes\": {\"flight_path_angle_deg\": -1.68},\n\"expected_outcome\": {\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\": 230800, \"peak_bondline_temperature_k\": 414.9, \"feasible\": true},\n\"uncertainty\": \"low\",\n\"reason_to_simulate\": \"Improves resolution of the convex front near its shallow end.\",\n\"requested_fidelity\": 0\n},\n{\n\"parent_id\": \"C-7fa59b50781c\",\n\"rationale\": \"Fill the gap between -2.0° and -2.2° at D=3.3852.\",\n\"parameter_changes\": {\"flight_path_angle_deg\": -2.1},\n\"expected_outcome\": {\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\": 239800, \"peak_bondline_temperature_k\": 408.5, \"feasible\": true},\n\"uncertainty\": \"low\",\n\"reason_to_simulate\": \"Interpolation between two evaluated points at the same D.\",\n\"requested_fidelity\": 0\n},\n{\n\"parent_id\": \"C-7fa59b50781c\",\n\"rationale\": \"Fill the gap between -2.2° and -2.5°.\",\n\"parameter_changes\": {\"flight_path_angle_deg\": -2.3},\n\"expected_outcome\": {\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\": 244350, \"peak_bondline_temperature_k\": 405.7, \"feasible\": true},\n\"uncertainty\": \"low\",\n\"reason_to_simulate\": \"Adds coverage in a sparsely sampled interval of the mid front.\",\n\"requested_fidelity\": 0\n},\n{\n\"parent_id\": \"C-60b626663373\",\n\"rationale\": \"Fill the gap between -2.5° and -3.0°, where D=3.3852 points are sparse.\",\n\"parameter_changes\": {\"flight_path_angle_deg\": -2.65},\n\"expected_outcome\": {\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\": 252500, \"peak_bondline_temperature_k\": 401.2, \"feasible\": true},\n\"uncertainty\": \"low\",\n\"reason_to_simulate\": \"Interpolation along a smooth section of the front.\",\n\"requested_fidelity\": 0\n},\n{\n\"parent_id\": \"C-abb511b4360b\",\n\"rationale\": \"Fill the gap between -2.5° and -3.0°, at the upper part of the interval.\",\n\"parameter_changes\": {\"flight_path_angle_deg\": -2.85},\n\"expected_outcome\": {\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\": 257200, \"peak_bondline_temperature_k\": 398.8, \"feasible\": true},\n\"uncertainty\": \"low\",\n\"reason_to_simulate\": \"Adds another mid-front point for a denser trade-off curve.\",\n\"requested_fidelity\": 0\n},\n{\n\"parent_id\": \"C-abb511b4360b\",\n\"rationale\": \"Fill the gap between -3.0° and -3.4°.\",\n\"parameter_changes\": {\"flight_path_angle_deg\": -3.2},\n\"expected_outcome\": {\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\": 265700, \"peak_bondline_temperature_k\": 394.8, \"feasible\": true},\n\"uncertainty\": \"low\",\n\"reason_to_simulate\": \"Interpolation at D=3.3852. The D=3.385 twin C-8e0603838c8c gives a close reference.\",\n\"requested_fidelity\": 0\n},\n{\n\"parent_id\": \"C-3981896fe111\",\n\"rationale\": \"Fill the gap between -3.4° and -3.5695° on the steep end.\",\n\"parameter_changes\": {\"flight_path_angle_deg\": -3.48},\n\"expected_outcome\": {\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\": 272400, \"peak_bondline_temperature_k\": 391.95, \"feasible\": true},\n\"uncertainty\": \"low\",\n\"reason_to_simulate\": \"Steep-end coverage at the corner D; max_g about 11.85, so the g margin is comfortable.\",\n\"requested_fidelity\": 0\n},\n{\n\"parent_id\": \"C-3981896fe111\",\n\"rationale\": \"Add a steep-end point close to the g limit, at -3.54°.\",\n\"parameter_changes\": {\"flight_path_angle_deg\": -3.54},\n\"expected_outcome\": {\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\": 273800, \"peak_bondline_temperature_k\": 391.4, \"feasible\": true},\n\"uncertainty\": \"low\",\n\"reason_to_simulate\": \"The g margin is about 0.4% here, so it should stay feasible; it improves resolution near the front end.\",\n\"requested_fidelity\": 0\n},\n{\n\"parent_id\": \"C-3981896fe111\",\n\"rationale\": \"Probe the steepest end of the front at -3.565°, close to the g cap of -3.5703°.\",\n\"parameter_changes\": {\"flight_path_angle_deg\": -3.565},\n\"expected_outcome\": {\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\": 274400, \"peak_bondline_temperature_k\": 391.15, \"feasible\": true},\n\"uncertainty\": \"medium\",\n\"reason_to_simulate\": \"Sits between C-a6a79568efb6 (-3.56°) and C-96e48a93fd32 (-3.5695°). Feasibility is likely because the g margin is around 5e-4.\",\n\"requested_fidelity\": 0\n},\n{\n\"parent_id\": \"C-96e48a93fd32\",\n\"rationale\": \"Push to -3.5700° at D=3.3852 to test whether the steep-end g cap is slightly beyond -3.5695° at this diameter.\",\n\"parameter_changes\": {\"flight_path_angle_deg\": -3.57},\n\"expected_outcome\": {\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\": 274590, \"peak_bondline_temperature_k\": 391.09, \"feasible\": true},\n\"uncertainty\": \"medium\",\n\"reason_to_simulate\": \"Marginal extension of the steepest feasible point. From the g trend, max_g should be about 11.9998, but the margin is only about 2e-5 to 1e-4, so it may fail.\",\n\"requested_fidelity\": 0\n}\n]\n}","ttft_ms":33273,"type":"result","duration_ms":62848,"uuid":"93b599b3-b403-425b-9b7c-530b2a41c8cc","ttft_stream_ms":1439,"time_to_request_ms":42,"first_content_frame_ms":1440,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
